# The other half of staleness, and the direction that is dangerous to get
# wrong. An alert fires on an element that by definition does not have focus.
# Treating "not the current focus" as "stale" would silence exactly the
# announcements a user least expects and most needs.
#
# The alert is Now priority, so it also drops the pending focus announcement
# for the button the user has already left. Both of those are correct.

node btn Button "Save"
node toast Alert "Battery low"
node other Button "Cancel"
focus btn
alert toast
focus other

expect
  Battery low
  Cancel, button
